            <div xml:id="d657">

                <pb facs="0816" n="804" sameAs="frus:frus1943v03/pg804"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00114A Pacific War/496: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Standley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-06-09T14:00:00+03:00">June 9, 1943—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 7:39 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>630. Department’s 365, May 26, 9 p.m., last paragraph. Foreign Office states that
                    a reply to the question concerning the several alternate routes for the movement
                    of supplies to American and Allied nationals detained by the Japs will be given
                    as soon as the American Government receives an answer from the Japanese
                    Government on the question.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Standley</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
